    {
      "id": "nest_namespace_ancestor_rg",
      "note": "The rg twin of seq 950027. Both walk with the same wrapped readdir and operand stat, so a fix applied to one and not the other is invisible until a case names it.",
      "seq": 950030,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "command": "rg ghost /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "/ghost/deep/g.txt:ghost\n",
        "stderr": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_namespace_ancestor_grep_is_a_directory",
      "note": "The synthesized row is a directory row, not merely a present one. Without -r grep refuses a directory operand, and it can only word that refusal if the stat it got back said directory; a file row would have made it read the path and fail as absent.",
      "seq": 950031,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "command": "grep -c ghost /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 2,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "grep: /ghost: Is a directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_namespace_ancestor_stat_format_spec",
      "note": "`%n` is the operand as typed, and the name override that fixed the default render must not reach it: the two fields answer different questions (`name=` is a basename for a file too) and only the default one was ever wrong.",
      "seq": 950032,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "command": "stat -c %n /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "/ghost\n",
        "stderr": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_namespace_ancestor_ls",
      "note": "ls, find and du already answered on a namespace-only ancestor; they are the reference the other verbs were made to agree with, so they are pinned here rather than left implied.",
