    {
      "id": "nest_hidden_mount_parent_grep",
      "note": "A session that hides the only mount under /ghost leaves nothing there to find, and the parent has to go back to reading as absent. The mount table is not session state, so the wrappers ask for the visible descendants: keyed on every descendant they answered an ordinary no-match here, which told the session /ghost exists when every other verb says it does not.",
      "seq": 950038,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "session": "blind",
      "command": "grep -r ghost /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 2,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "grep: /ghost: No such file or directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_hidden_mount_parent_rg",
      "seq": 950039,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "session": "blind",
      "command": "rg ghost /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 2,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "rg: /ghost: No such file or directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_hidden_mount_parent_grep_operand",
      "note": "The operand stat is the other half: seq 950031 gets a directory row here, and under the hide it must get nothing rather than a row saying the path is there.",
      "seq": 950040,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "session": "blind",
      "command": "grep -c ghost /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 2,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "grep: /ghost: No such file or directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_hidden_mount_parent_stat",
      "note": "What the answer above is required to match. stat reads the namespace through the dispatcher, which filters the hides already, so it is the verb the search pair had drifted away from.",
      "seq": 950041,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "session": "blind",
      "command": "stat /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 1,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "stat: /ghost: No such file or directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_hidden_mount_sibling_still_searchable",
      "note": "The hide withholds one mount, not the session's whole search surface.",
      "seq": 950042,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "session": "blind",
      "command": "grep -r top /data",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "/data/top.txt:top\n",
        "stderr": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_namespace_ancestor_cat",
      "note": "A read command decides what a directory is at one chokepoint, and it knew two kinds: the explicit stat row and the implicit prefix a keyed backend answers a readdir for. A namespace-only mount parent is the third, belonging to no backend at all, and without it every read command called the path missing while stat, file, ls, du, find, tree and test -d all called it a directory. Fixing the chokepoint fixed the whole family at once, so these cases are a sample of it rather than a list.",
      "seq": 950043,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "command": "cat /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 1,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "cat: /ghost: Is a directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_namespace_ancestor_wc",
      "seq": 950044,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "command": "wc -l /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 1,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "wc: /ghost: Is a directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_namespace_ancestor_head",
      "seq": 950045,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "command": "head /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 1,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "head: /ghost: Is a directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_namespace_ancestor_tail",
      "seq": 950046,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "command": "tail /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 1,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "tail: /ghost: Is a directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_namespace_ancestor_md5sum",
      "note": "The stream half of the chokepoint rather than the stat half, so both are covered: the checksum family reads through dir_aware_stream where cat reads through dir_aware_stat.",
      "seq": 950047,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "command": "md5sum /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 1,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "md5sum: /ghost: Is a directory\n"
