    {
      "id": "nest_namespace_ancestor_cat_keeps_siblings",
      "note": "GNU names the directory and reads the rest of the line. Reporting it as a missing operand did that too, so the wording is the whole difference and the operand handling must not regress with it.",
      "seq": 950049,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "command": "cat /ghost /data/top.txt",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 1,
        "stdout": "top\n",
        "stderr": "cat: /ghost: Is a directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_hidden_mount_parent_cat",
      "note": "The hide outranks the directory synthesis, and it comes for free: the dispatcher the chokepoint asks already filters what the session may be told about, so the operand falls back to the absence every other verb reports for it.",
      "seq": 950050,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "session": "blind",
      "command": "cat /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 1,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "cat: /ghost: No such file or directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_hidden_mount_parent_wc",
      "seq": 950051,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "session": "blind",
      "command": "wc -l /ghost",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 1,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "wc: /ghost: No such file or directory\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_hidden_mount_root_listing",
      "note": "The name plane's own leak, one layer below the verbs above. A mount name is derived for every ancestor segment it runs through, and the visibility test was applied to the segment rather than to the mount, so a session that hid /ghost/deep still learned /ghost from a root listing while every verb applied to /ghost answered ENOENT. A hide is subtree-closed, so testing the deeper path can only withhold a segment, never grant one.",
      "seq": 950052,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "session": "blind",
      "command": "ls /",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "data\ndev\n",
        "stderr": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "nest_root_listing_unfiltered",
      "note": "The control for the case above: with no session bound the segment is still owed and still listed.",
      "seq": 950053,
      "targets": [
        "ram-nested"
      ],
      "command": "ls /",
      "expect": {
